35,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The grant terms are restrictive, and the road closures are a significant risk for any mobile service. We cannot rely on external transport.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Yumi,,Oh no! I found out that the outer wards lost their bus links! People there are really struggling to reach us. We have to help!,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,George,,As I suspected. The funding is fragmented. We have money for equipment but not for the running costs to keep it moving.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,May,,See? The outreach stops were actually a hit! Forty people per session! We just stopped because we didn't look at the data.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I found that we don't have any staff trained to supervise new types of programs. If we add more, the current staff will just... break.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Yumi, if the buses are gone and the roads close in winter, a centralized service is useless. But a mobile one is too risky.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"But we can't just leave them! @May, if the outreach was popular, maybe we can find a way to bring the library to them?","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,George,,Not with the current budget structure. We would run out of fuel and maintenance money by month fourteen. We need a sustainable model.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,May,,Then why not use the partner-run model from six years ago? It's still running without our help! That's the definition of sustainable.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"But... who will manage it? I saw the register. We have volunteers, but no staff can actually supervise them. It's too much pressure.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Daisuke is right. If we depend on a few over-stressed staff, the system collapses when one person gets sick. We need independence.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"I just can't ignore the people in the outer wards. If we don't do something, the library is only for people who can afford cars!","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,George,,"We must choose a proposal that doesn't rely on a recurring grant that disappears. A fixed-cost, low-maintenance expansion is the only way.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,May,,Exactly. Stop trying to invent a new wheel. The partner-led community hubs are already working. We just need to officially support them.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I guess if the community manages it, the staff won't have to do everything. That might... actually work.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,I agree. A distributed model using existing community infrastructure reduces our dependency on roads and fragile grant cycles.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Yumi,,"As long as it reaches those outer wards! If the hubs are where the people are, then I'm all for it!","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,George,,"It avoids the budget cliff. If the community provides the space, we only provide the books and the initial setup.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,May,,Finally! We're actually using our brains and our history. I'm almost proud of you all.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,I feel a bit better about that. As long as we don't just dump the work on the librarians.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
